# {{project.title}}

{{project.description}}.

Plain Java library for the axiz ecosystem (layer 1): it depends on no structure, so it can be used
from Spring, Quarkus or plain Java. Build with `./mvnw verify` (enforcer rules and tests);
`./mvnw -Pquality verify` adds the format check, Checkstyle, Error Prone + NullAway and coverage, as CI does.
`ci.yaml` uses `lib-build@v2.0.0` to build and retain signed Maven staging bytes. It receives the
version, source commit and optional framework candidate identity. `deploy.yaml` independently
promotes a completed successful producer run using its attempt and external manifest SHA-256;
it never executes Maven. Release-please prepares a draft; promotion retains the signed manifest
before publishing that release. Use separate Nexus read credentials for builds and
`NEXUS_PUBLISH_USERNAME/PASSWORD` for promotion. `version.txt` and `.release-please-manifest.json` hold the last released version (`0.0.0`:
nothing released yet); the pom holds the next one (`0.1.0-SNAPSHOT`). The first release is `0.1.0` (`initial-version` in
`release-please-config.json`); later ones follow Conventional Commits.

## Rules

- Public API documented with Javadoc; packages `@NullMarked` (JSpecify).
- No Spring, Quarkus, AWS SDK v1 nor test libraries in compile scope (the parent enforces it).
- Immutable values (records), no global state, no `System.out`.
